<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Massina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Macina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Massina, or Macina, is a region of the inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, a seasonally flooded plain around Mopti and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djenne">Djenné</a>. Long home to Fulbe herders as well as farmers and fishermen, it was ruled by Fulbe ardo chiefs under Bambara overlords until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seku-amadu">Seku Amadu</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> of 1818 founded the Massina Empire, which the Toucouleur Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">El Hadj Umar Tall</a> conquered in 1862.</p></div>
